<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-1557] Storage layer sync mechanism doesn&apos;t fail gracefully </title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-1557</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;During storage sync mechanism get/save operations are performed  for a list of notes in &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/blob/master/zeppelin-zengine/src/main/java/org/apache/zeppelin/notebook/repo/NotebookRepoSync.java#L231&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;. If one of operations fail, the whole sync returns with failure. In order to handle it gracefully, we need to catch exceptions and go on. &lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="13012875">ZEPPELIN-1557</key>
            <summary>Storage layer sync mechanism doesn&apos;t fail gracefully </summary>
